---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// Seven blocks, one job each. The page carries no number at all, which is the
// point: every figure it could print would be invented, and an audit that
// sells itself on a made-up percentage is arguing against its own product.
// What it shows instead is the classification, which is the actual output.

const paths = [
  { k: 'AI',       t: 'Work that benefits from judgement, context and flexibility.',                  tone: 'live'  },
  { k: 'Software', t: 'Work with clear rules that traditional automation can handle better.',         tone: 'ink'   },
  { k: 'Human',    t: 'Work that requires judgement, accountability or should remain with a person.', tone: 'plain' },
  { k: 'Not yet',  t: 'Work that may become automatable, but is not reliable enough today.',          tone: 'ember' },
];

const blocker = [
  'A missing integration',
  'Not enough real cases yet',
  'A business decision nobody has taken',
  'A change to access and permissions',
];
---

<Base
  title="The KYDE Audit, Where the Work Should Run"
  description="We take one complete business process and map the work inside it: what should run with AI, what belongs in conventional software, what stays with people, and what is not ready yet. Dated, with the blocker and the owner on everything that is held back."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main>
    <!-- ══════════ 1 · THE ARGUMENT ══════════ -->
    <section class="relative bg-bg-1 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-grid opacity-[0.06] pointer-events-none"></div>
      <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 pt-36 pb-24 md:pt-48 md:pb-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h1 class="hero-h1 text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-ink-0 uppercase tracking-tight leading-[1.05] mb-10">
            AI should do<br />real work.
          </h1>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
            <p>
              AI is entering every company. But the opportunity is not another chatbot. It is giving software the ability to take on real work.
            </p>
            <p class="text-ink-0">The question is: what work should it actually do?</p>
            <p>
              KYDE takes one complete business process and maps the work inside it. We show what should run with AI, what belongs in traditional software, what should stay with people, and what is simply not ready yet.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-10 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-1">
            One process area <span class="text-ink-3" aria-hidden="true">·</span> Fixed price <span class="text-ink-3" aria-hidden="true">·</span> A dated answer
          </p>
          <div class="mt-10">
            <button onclick="openModal()" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-cta-ink px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:bg-cta-hover transition-all">
              Start your audit →
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 2 · THE MAP ══════════ -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3 mb-14">
          <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">The map</span>
          <span class="fig-label">FIG.1</span>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-ink-0 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          See what your process can actually run.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-14">
          <p>
            We follow one process from beginning to end, across the people, decisions and systems involved.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-0">For each part of the work, we determine the right way to run it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-line-0 divide-y divide-line-0 md:divide-y-0 md:grid md:grid-cols-4 md:divide-x">
          {paths.map(({ k, t, tone }) => (
            <div class="px-6 py-8 md:px-7">
              <span class:list={[
                "inline-block font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] px-2.5 py-1 mb-5",
                tone === 'live'  ? 'text-live border border-live/30 bg-live/[0.08]' : '',
                tone === 'ink'   ? 'text-ink-0 border border-line-1' : '',
                tone === 'ember' ? 'text-ember border border-ember/30 bg-ember/[0.08]' : '',
                tone === 'plain' ? 'text-ink-1 border border-line-0' : '',
              ]}>{k}</span>
              <p class="text-base text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">{t}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p class="mt-10 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
          The result is a clear map of what can run now, what needs to change, and what is likely to become possible next.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-[10px] text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">FIG.1 · The four paths a piece of work can take.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 3 · IT HAS A DATE ══════════ -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-ink-0 mb-8">
            The answer has a date.
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              AI is moving quickly. A task that is not reliable enough today may be ready in six months.
            </p>
            <p>
              So we do not give you a static AI assessment. Every part of the process gets a current status and, where possible, a date to reassess it.
            </p>
            <p>
              When you come back later, you can see what changed and what became possible.
            </p>
            <p class="text-ink-0">A living map of what your business can actually automate.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 4 · WHAT IS IN THE WAY ══════════ -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-0 md:divide-x md:divide-line-0 [&>*:first-child]:md:pr-12 [&>*:last-child]:md:pl-12 lg:[&>*:first-child]:pr-16 lg:[&>*:last-child]:pl-16">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-ink-0 mb-8">
              We look at what has to happen before it can run.
            </h2>
            <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                A process may be ready for AI but blocked by a missing integration. It may need more real cases, a business decision or a change to access and permissions.
              </p>
              <p class="text-ink-0">We identify the blocker and the owner.</p>
              <p>
                At the same time, we look at the infrastructure the work would run on: your systems, identity, network, data and existing automation.
              </p>
              <p>
                So you know what to automate, what to change, and what to leave alone.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col justify-center">
            <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-2 mb-6">What a blocker looks like</p>
            <ul class="border border-line-0 divide-y divide-line-0">
              {blocker.map((b) => (
                <li class="px-5 py-4 text-base text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">{b}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 5 · THE READOUT ══════════ -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-ink-0 mb-8">
            A plan you can act on.
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed mb-12">
            <p>
              At the end of the audit, you receive a dated readout of the complete process. It shows where AI, software and people belong, what can run today, what is holding the rest back, and what should be reassessed later.
            </p>
            <p>
              Built to be useful to the people making the investment decision, not only to the people who ran the workshop.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-snug text-ink-0">
            Know what to build. Know what to wait for. Know what to leave alone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ 6 · START ══════════ -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-0 md:divide-x md:divide-line-0 [&>*:first-child]:md:pr-12 [&>*:last-child]:md:pl-12 lg:[&>*:first-child]:pr-16 lg:[&>*:last-child]:pl-16">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-ink-0 mb-8">
              Start with one process.
            </h2>
            <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                Choose a process where people spend significant time moving information, making decisions or working across systems.
              </p>
              <p>
                We scope it with you and give you the timeline and price before anything begins.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col justify-center">
            <dl class="border border-line-0 divide-y divide-line-0 mb-8">
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 px-6 py-5">
                <dt class="text-base text-ink-1">A single team</dt>
                <dd class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-0 whitespace-nowrap">about three days</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 px-6 py-5">
                <dt class="text-base text-ink-1">A department</dt>
                <dd class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-0 whitespace-nowrap">about two weeks</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="text-base text-ink-1 leading-relaxed mb-10">
              The audit fee comes off your first automation project with KYDE.
            </p>
            <button onclick="openModal()" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white text-cta-ink px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.12em] hover:bg-cta-hover transition-all w-fit">
              Book a 30-minute scoping call →
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════ CLOSER ══════════ -->
    <section class="bg-bg-0">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-ink-0 mb-6">
            The next generation of software does not just answer questions.<br />It does the work.
          </h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed mb-12 mx-auto max-w-2xl">
            KYDE helps you understand where that work should run, and builds the workers to run it.
          </p>
          <button onclick="openModal()" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white px-8 py-4 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-cta-ink hover:bg-cta-hover transition-all">
            Talk to us →
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
